cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Exoplanet Science Lab in work that leads to a publication, please cite the software with the
  version you used, and the papers of the methods your analysis relied on (docs/METHODS.md lists them by
  section; docs/references.bib holds the BibTeX; the function methodsParagraph in src/core/methodsText.js
  writes the list for a given session).
type: software
title: "Exoplanet Science Lab"
abstract: >-
  Transit, radial-velocity, timing, phase-curve and photometry analysis for exoplanet observations that runs
  in the browser, with a nested sampler, a session format for reproducible fits, and the same core callable
  from Python.
authors:
  - family-names: Pearson
    given-names: Kyle A.
version: "0.2.0"
url: "https://exoplanet.science"
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - transit photometry
  - radial velocities
  - transit timing
  - nested sampling
  - Bayesian inference
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pearsonkyle/Exoplanet-Science-Lab"
